📘 Volatility Analysis Blueprint (3-Level Version)

🎯 Purpose
The Volatility module measures the consistency vs instability of customer emotional resonance (ERI/NES) over time.
Unlike momentum or trend, it is non-directional — it purely captures emotional turbulence or emotional predictability.

It enables CX leaders to understand how stable or chaotic an experience feels emotionally — regardless of whether it is positive or negative.

🧮 Computation
Volatility is calculated as the standard deviation of ERI scores over a defined rolling time window (e.g., 30, 60, or 90 days):
ERI_volatility = standard deviation(ERI_timeseries)

✅ Higher standard deviation = greater emotional instability.
✅ Lower standard deviation = greater emotional predictability.

📊 3-Level Volatility Classification

| **Volatility Score Range** | **Tier**              | **Label**                                     | **Interpretation** |
| -------------------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |
| 0–15                       | ✅ Stable              | Emotion is predictable and consistent         |                    |
| 16–45                      | ⚠ Fluctuating         | Noticeable emotional movement (not stable)    |                    |
| 46+                        | 🔴 Highly Fluctuating | Erratic, unstable, chaotic emotional behavior |                    |

✅ Interpretation Tips:
- Stable: Customers feel consistently similar emotions over time (good or bad).
- Fluctuating: Emotions are shifting — could signal improvement, decline, or instability.
- Highly Fluctuating: Sentiment is extremely volatile — major risk for unpredictable CX outcomes.

🧠 Strategic Insights by Volatility Tier

| **Volatility Tier**   | **Meaning**                             | **Strategic Focus**                                                 |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| ✅ Stable              | Predictable emotional landscape         | Maintain or systematically improve (depending on sentiment quality) |
| ⚠ Fluctuating         | Emerging or unstable emotional movement | Investigate drivers; stabilize experience                           |
| 🔴 Highly Fluctuating | Dangerous instability                   | Immediate diagnosis needed; system/process breakdown likely         |


💡 Professional Note
✅ Volatility ≠ Good or Bad by itself:
 A process can be consistently bad (stable negative) or consistently good (stable positive).
✅ Volatility measures predictability, not quality.

